VaR (Value at risk): 
The potential losses(in value) a portfolio can incurr, 
in a specific time period, with a given confidence.
                                                                                  CVaR (Conditional value at risk) / ES (Expected shortfall):
                                                                                  The average of losses beyond the VaR threshold for a given
                                                                                  confidence level.
                                                                                  Captures severity of losses in the tail of the distribution.
                                                                                  Satisfy properties of a coherent risk measure.
                                                                                  

Limitation:
VaR doesn't capture the severity of losses beyond the threshold.
Not a coherent risk measure.


                                    [A coherent risk measure is a mathematical framework in quantitative
                                    finance and actuarial science used to evaluate portfolio risk in 
                                    a consistent, logical manner.]
